## 7. Important no-go

It is inconsistent to demand all three of the following without an additional
argument:

1. the physical state has nonzero closure curvature;
2. its linearized first-order operator is an ordinary nilpotent differential;
3. the curvature acts nontrivially through the standard twisted-differential
   identity.

At least one clause must be weakened or the curvature must act trivially in the
chosen representation.

